# Horizontal cutting plane at z=0, normal = (0,0,+1)
#
# Regression test: the triangle normal is exactly UnitZ, so when retriangulate
# computes the rotation axis via n.cross(UnitZ) it gets the zero vector.
# After Bug 2's fix (special-casing this as angle=0 / identity rotation) this
# should work correctly.  Before the fix it produced NaN rotation matrices.
#
# Used as knife against clay_unit_cube: should cut the cube into top/bottom halves.

v -3 -3 0
v  3 -3 0
v  3  3 0
v -3  3 0

f 1 2 3
f 1 3 4
